1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,240
Before handing a key to an AI agent, check what it can actually do.

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,440
I built Key Scope for NEAR Hackathon.

3
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:08,400
Here is my example policy.

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,160
Testnet.

5
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:10,160
One receiver.

6
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:11,360
One allowed method.

7
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:12,920
And a gas allowance cap.

8
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:15,520
The account is a public third party example.

9
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:17,360
This policy is illustrative.

10
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:20,800
Not a statement about what its owner intended.

11
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:25,680
Now I run the audit against the bundled snapshot.

12
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:28,640
The result is fail, with the finding all methods.

13
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:29,640
In NEAR,

14
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:33,440
An empty function call method list means every method on that receiver,
not

15
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:34,440
zero methods.

16
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:37,640
The command exits one because it detected a mismatch.

17
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:39,600
That is a successful rejection.

18
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:40,600
Not a crash.

19
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,080
Full access recovery keys elsewhere on the account are left alone.

20
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:52,000
I also queried the public Testnet RPC with finalized data for this demo.

21
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,760
The saved response includes a new block hash, height, and capture time,

22
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:57,400
replaying that fresh

23
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,800
response finds the same mismatch.

24
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:03,480
This is trusted RPC data, not a cryptographic proof.

25
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,160
A pass would only describe the observed block.

26
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,960
Permissions can change afterwards.

27
00:01:11,067 --> 00:01:12,727
All 20 tests pass.

28
00:01:12,727 --> 00:01:15,327
They cover one yocto above the allowance limit,

29
00:01:15,327 --> 00:01:19,007
full access, unrestricted methods, missing evidence,

30
00:01:19,007 --> 00:01:20,647
and command exit codes.

31
00:01:20,647 --> 00:01:23,887
The positive case is a labeled synthetic restricted key,

32
00:01:23,887 --> 00:01:26,927
bad input or an RPC failure returns unknown.

33
00:01:26,927 --> 00:01:27,927
Never pass.

34
00:01:27,927 --> 00:01:29,687
This tool audits permissions.

35
00:01:29,687 --> 00:01:33,647
It does not enforce a wallet policy, inspect contract code,

36
00:01:33,647 --> 00:01:37,287
or promise asset safety, clone the public repository,

37
00:01:37,287 --> 00:01:41,527
run npm test, then npm run demo to reproduce the rejection.
